y":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-01-30T22:33:13Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T14:27:39Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\ntested in 4.3\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, 4.3 stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nI was testing a conveyor belt game and i had to check when a \"ore\" exited the belt to make it stop moving. Turns out the RigidBody2D was not being detected to the signal.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa31deab-a94f-48f2-aee0-c46ed9db17b9)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/274bf3b3-e141-4e5e-9766-001976952f37)\n\nTo solve this bug, i changed it to a characterbody2d and it worked. In my mind, they are a \"body\"\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/187cfbe0-8f6a-4b86-a75f-45abc630d943)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nto test the bug, just change the iron ore to a rigidbody2d provided in the project below\nor, check if a body entered/exited an area with a rigidbody2d\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[conveyor-belt-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18609403/conveyor-belt-test.zip)\n\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102214/timeline","performe